Essential status questions
- What is the current case status and any confirmed or expected hearing/trial dates?
- Are there any upcoming deadlines I must meet (motions, responses, disclosures)? What are the dates?
- What is our overall strategy (defend, settle, limit exposure)? How does that affect what evidence we need?

Discovery / evidence-specific questions
- Is discovery fully closed? If not, what remains to be produced or obtained?
- Which documents or evidence would be most persuasive at the hearing? (prioritize)
- Are there any outstanding requests to the opposing party (document requests, interrogatories, admissions)? Should we file motions to compel?
- Do we need depositions or sworn witness statements before the hearing?
- Do we need subpoenas for third-party records (banks, employers, vendors)? If so, who should I identify?

Document collection checklist (gather these now if you haven’t)
- Contract(s), amendments, exhibits, and any written communications about the contract (emails, texts, signed notes)
- Invoices, payment records, bank statements, receipts, canceled checks
- Employment records, performance reviews, termination notices (if relevant)
- Any notices, demand letters, or service documents received
- Calendars, meeting notes, and contemporaneous notes you made
- Witness names and short summaries of what each can attest to
- Any audio/video evidence, screenshots, or metadata (keep originals)

Evidence handling & authenticity
- How should I preserve original documents and digital evidence (formats, backups)?
- Do we need forensics or an expert to authenticate electronic records?
- How should exhibits be labeled and organized for filing and the hearing?

Legal motions & strategy tied to evidence
- Would filing pre-hearing motions (e.g., motion in limine, to exclude evidence) help?
- Should we seek any protective orders or limitations on opposing evidence?
- Is there benefit to an early settlement demand or mediation using current evidence?

Practical next steps / client responsibilities
- Which documents do you want me to collect right away? Which are lower priority?
- Do you want me to draft witness summaries or sworn declarations?
- What should I avoid doing (e.g., contacting certain people, deleting any communications)?
- What will you (attorney) handle vs. what you expect me to produce?

Costs & timeline
- Estimated time and cost to obtain additional evidence (depositions, subpoenas, experts)
- How much lead time do we need to get new evidence admitted at the hearing?

Closing / confirmation
- After I gather X items, can we have a short meeting (phone/video) to review before the next deadline?
- Is anything else you need from me immediately?

If you want, I can:
- Draft an email to Robert Kim listing these questions (ready to send or save as a draft)
- Search your inbox for emails from Robert Kim or other legal/court senders and forward them to vince2000@gmail.com
- Create a concise checklist/draft you can print or store

