Thanks — this is helpful context. I can help in a few ways. First, here’s a concise, prioritized checklist of questions you should ask your attorney (Robert Kim) to make sure you’re ready for the next legal steps and to determine whether you need more evidence.

Key questions to ask your attorney
- Case status & timeline
  - What is the current status of the case and the next court date(s)?
  - What are the upcoming deadlines I need to be aware of (motions, filings, responses)?
- Evidence & discovery
  - Is the evidence we already have sufficient for the upcoming hearing?
  - Are there any gaps in the discovery that could hurt our position?
  - Should we request additional documents from the opposing party (or third parties)? If so, what specifically?
  - Do we need subpoenas for documents or witness testimony? Who should be subpoenaed?
- Witnesses & testimony
  - Which witnesses will be critical, and do we have written statements or affidavits from them?
  - Should we depose anyone else before the hearing?
- Expert testimony
  - Do we need an expert (e.g., valuation, contract interpretation)? If yes, how quickly can one be retained and prepared?
- Motions & strategy
  - Are there any pre-hearing motions we should file (e.g., motion to compel, summary judgment, protective order)?
  - What is the recommended legal strategy for the forthcoming hearing?
- Risk & settlement
  - What are our realistic best-case and worst-case outcomes?
  - Is settlement advisable at this stage? If so, what terms should we consider?
- Costs & timing
  - What additional costs/time would collecting more evidence incur vs. potential benefit?
- Your role & preparation
  - What should I do to prepare (documents to gather, timeline of events to write up, people to contact)?
  - What will you handle, and what do you need me to do immediately?
- Administrative
  - Confirm your contact details and fee arrangement for next steps.
  - Do you expect to need more time to respond to service or filings, and can we get extensions if needed?

Sample short email to your attorney
Subject: Questions about evidence and next steps — [Your Name] / housing court case

Body:
