I pulled together a focused list of questions and a short checklist you can use with Robert Kim to decide whether you need more evidence before the next court date — plus a ready-to-send email you can use (or save as a draft). Tell me if you want me to send or draft the email for you.

Key questions to ask your attorney
- Timeline & deadlines
  - What is the exact next court date and all upcoming deadlines (response, pretrial filings, evidence/exhibit lists)?
  - Do we have time to gather additional evidence before that date? If not, what can be done afterward?
  - Can we ask the court for an extension if we need more time?

- Case posture & strategy
  - What is our overall strategy at the next hearing (status conference, motion hearing, trial readiness)?
  - What issues does the court expect us to address at the next date?
  - Are we better off seeking settlement/mediation now or proceeding?

- Evidence you need
  - Which specific documents or records would be most persuasive (contracts, payroll records, termination notices, emails, texts, invoices, bank statements)?
  - Do we need original documents or are certified copies / screenshots acceptable?
  - Are there particular dates, transactions, or communications you want me to prioritize collecting?

- Witnesses & testimony
  - Do we need witness statements or declarations now? If so, who should I ask to provide them?
  - Should any witnesses be subpoenaed to produce documents or attend the hearing?
  - Do we need expert testimony (e.g., damages, accounting) and what is the timeline to retain an expert?

- Discovery & procedural steps
  - Are there outstanding discovery requests or obligations we should pursue (interrogatories, requests for production, depositions)?
  - Do we need to move to compel production or take any immediate discovery actions?
  - Are there any privilege or confidentiality issues to be aware of?

- Authentication & chain of custody
  - Will any documents need notarization, certification, or proof of authenticity?
  - If digital evidence (texts, social, logs), how should I preserve and provide it (screenshots, metadata, export formats)?

