Do you want me to draft and send an email to your lawyer Robert Kim, or just give a list of questions you can use in your conversation? I can also save a draft for you if you prefer.

Below are recommended questions to ask your attorney (organized and ready to copy into an email or call script), plus a short sample email you can send or I can draft for you.

Suggested questions to ask your attorney
- Case status & timeline
  - What is the next court date or deadline I should be aware of?
  - What must be completed before that date (filings, evidence, witness disclosures)?
- Evidence & documents
  - What specific documents do you need from me before the next hearing?
  - Are there any documents we still need to obtain from third parties (bank statements, employer records, call/text/email logs)?
  - Do any documents need authentication or affidavits to admit them at hearing?
- Witnesses & statements
  - Do we need witness statements or affidavits now? Which witnesses are most important?
  - Should I prepare a timeline or written summary of events for you to use at hearing?
- Discovery & outstanding items
  - Is discovery fully closed? If not, what remains outstanding and how do we force production if needed?
  - Are there discovery deficiencies worth filing a motion to compel?
- Motions & strategy
  - Are there any motions you recommend filing before the hearing (motion in limine, summary judgment, compel, sanctions)?
  - What is the defense/opposing party likely to argue, and how should we prepare to rebut it?
- Practical courtroom prep
  - What exhibits should I bring and how many copies are needed?
  - Do you prefer electronically submitted exhibits or paper binders? Any formatting requirements?
  - Will I need to testify? If so, should we schedule a prep session?
- Evidence preservation & subpoenas
  - Do we need to subpoena records or witnesses now? How long will that take?
  - Are there any steps I must take immediately to preserve evidence?
- Costs & retainer
  - Any expected additional costs for subpoenas, expert reports, filings, or court fees?
  - Do we need to adjust the retainer?
- Settlement & alternatives
  - Is settlement a realistic option before the next date? If so, what terms should I consider?
- Next steps for you (the client)
  - What should I do right now (gather receipts, transcripts, emails, prepare timeline, contact witnesses)?
  - Anything I must not do or say to the opposing party while we prepare?

