- Preserve all communications and files (don’t delete emails, texts, Slack messages). Consider exporting backups.  
- If anything is on a personal device, make a copy and note chain-of-custody.  
- Confirm with your attorney that privilege logs are accurate and no privileged documents were inadvertently produced.  
- Make a simple, dated timeline of relevant events (one page) to review with your attorney.  
- Note witnesses’ availability and any contact constraints (e.g., confidentiality agreements).

Questions about costs & logistics
- What are estimated costs for additional discovery, depositions, or experts?  
- How will we handle subpoenaing third-party records (bank records, phone records)?  
- Do you want me to coordinate witness availability or collect documents and upload them to you?

Short phone script to call your attorney
