- Should I obtain sworn witness statements or sworn affidavits? Which witnesses matter most?
- Do we need an expert (e.g., damages expert, accountant)? If so, when do we engage them?
- Should we consider filing any pre-hearing motions now (summary judgment, exclusion of evidence, etc.)?
- Do we need subpoenas for documents or testimony? If yes, who should be subpoenaed and by when?
- How should I preserve and label my evidence (preferred file formats, chronology, index)?
- What is the timeline from now until the hearing — any filing deadlines, exchange deadlines, or court appearances?
- Any tactical advice about what to avoid saying or sharing publicly?
- Can we meet/call to review the evidence and prepare testimony or a hearing outline?

3) Documents you may want to prepare/attach
- Contract(s) at issue (signed pages, amendments)
- All communications with the former employer (emails, texts, letters)
- Invoices, receipts, bank statements or payment records
- Discovery responses and any produced documents
- Timeline summary (one-page chronological events)
- Court papers (complaint, summons, discovery notices, any orders)
- Any documents that show attempts to resolve the dispute

