I see from your memory that you’re in a contract-dispute case with hearings coming up and you want to be ready — I can help you prepare questions for your attorney and/or draft an email to Robert Kim. Which would you like me to do? I can: (A) give a short checklist and questions to ask your lawyer now; (B) draft a concise email you can send; or (C) draft and send the email (I’ll need the attorney’s email address or confirmation to use one I find in your inbox).

Below are (1) a focused checklist of documents to gather, (2) suggested questions to ask Robert Kim, and (3) a ready-to-send email draft you can modify. Tell me which action to take next.

1) Documents to gather now (high priority)
- Original contract and any amendments.
- All emails/texts/messages between you and the former employer about the contract or performance.
- Invoices, payment records, bank statements, canceled checks, payroll records showing amounts/dates.
- Work product or deliverables demonstrating performance (files, timestamps, commit logs).
- Any written warnings, performance reviews, or termination notices.
- Discovery responses, interrogatories, and documents already exchanged.
- Pleadings filed by both parties and case number/court date(s).
- Timeline of events (chronological bullets with dates).
- Names and contact info for possible witnesses (co-workers, supervisors, clients).
- Any expert reports or appraisals (if applicable).
- Photos/screenshots, metadata if possible (showing timestamps).

2) Key questions to ask your attorney (prioritize the first 5 if time is short)
- Do we need additional evidence before the next hearing/response deadline? If so, what specifically?
- Which documents or witnesses would have the biggest impact on our position?
- Are there outstanding discovery items we should request or compel?
- Do you recommend depositions of any witnesses before the hearing? If yes, who and why?
- What is the deadline for our response or any motions? (Confirm exact dates.)
- Do we need an expert? If so, on what issue and by when must they be retained?
- Are there procedural steps (motions in limine, pretrial disclosures, exhibit lists) we should prepare now?
- What are the risks if we don’t obtain more evidence vs. if we do?
- How long will additional discovery take and does it affect the hearing schedule?
- Estimate of costs and time to pursue more evidence (budget/benefit).
- Do you want me to prepare an affidavit or summary of facts for you to submit?
- Anything I should not do (e.g., contact certain people, delete messages)?

